er than established actual effects.","name":"possible_local_policy_implications","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change is the subject of an existing application received by the SFC before 28 November 2025 for which no approval or authorisation had been granted at that date, under the stated transition assumption.","name":"legacy_pending_application","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and (>= assessment_date (date 2025-11-28)) home_requirements_met (not novel_features) (not complex_features) (not possible_local_policy_implications) (not legacy_pending_application))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and covered_ucits covered_material_change)"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Do the revised FAQs add a separate home-supervision test or specify how home compliance must be evidenced?","Can a pending applicant withdraw its application and implement the same change under the new relief?","Which existing provisions determine whether prior approval remains required where this relief is unavailable?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] For the selected control, 'eligibility for removal of SFC prior approval under item (ii)', true means an in-scope material investment change satisfies the circular's stated relief conditions under the specified timing assumptions. False means this test does not establish relief; it does not itself establish a prior-approval duty, prohibition, licence possession or non-compliance. Unknown inputs remain unknown. Qualifying changes receive prior-approval relief while remaining subject to applicable notification, filing and post-vetting arrangements.","subject":"Conditional prior-approval relief for one material UCITS investment change"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.00787ab10a284a072204b281","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"54612ae3c156b14377db11a50ef6d40e45714d5e570bb22c9e272e4bd80128ec","candidate_id":"candidate.abf152a8ba614429aeca78213d1281ed","commitment":"074087c89e3a3304960f612e6ee314578afc64d2ebb64a65f316d6edce81bc25","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.074087c89e3a3304960f612e","order":1,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The express effective date governs the general statement that the measures take immediate effect.","Whether an existing application remains unapproved is assessed at the effective date.","For this proposal, retention in the existing approval process excludes the pending application from the new removal of prior approval.","The stated home-supervision rationale does not add a distinct approval or supervision test to item (ii)'s express home-jurisdiction compliance condition.","The absent FAQs may qualify implementation; this is a reading of the supplied text only."],"citations":[{"quote":"The key streamlined measures cover the following post-authorisation matters:","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},{"quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"quote":"1 For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"}],"distinction":"This reading tests eligibility for the selected removal of prior approval. The strongest unresolved alternative concerns pending applications: 'existing ... process' could retain only procedure while permitting the new substantive relaxation. That alternative would change the outcome for an otherwise qualifying pre-date pending application, but the packet does not establish it sufficiently to select a second executable rule. Failure of this eligibility test alone does not prove that approval is legally required.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The fund is a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled collective investment scheme authorised as UK UCITS.","name":"defined_ucits_fund","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change is a post-authorisation matter for the fund.","name":"post_authorisation_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u3.575"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change is material and concerns the fund's investment objective, policy or restriction.","name":"material_investment_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"Date as of which availability of the selected removal of prior approval is assessed.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The selected change complies with the fund's applicable home-jurisdiction requirements.","name":"home_requirements_met","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change involves novel product features.","name":"novel_features","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change involves complex product features.","name":"complex_features","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The selected change may have local policy implications; this asks about possibility, not only established actual effects.","name":"possible_local_policy_implications","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"An application concerning the selected change was received by the SFC before 28 November 2025 and had received neither approval nor authorisation by that date.","name":"pending_pre_effective_application","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696","d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and (>= assessment_date (date 2025-11-28)) home_requirements_met (not (or novel_features complex_features possible_local_policy_implications)) (not pending_pre_effective_application))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and defined_ucits_fund post_authorisation_change material_investment_change)"},"local_id":"removal_eligibility","questions":["Does the transition preserve substantive approval requirements as assumed, or only administrative processing?","What further qualifications do the referenced FAQs place on the selected removal?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within scope, true means the selected material investment change qualifies for removal of SFC prior approval under item (ii), on the proposed transition reading: the assessment is on or after 28 November 2025, home requirements are met, no novel or complex product features or possible local policy implications are involved, and no pre-effective pending application retains the existing process. False means this particular removal is unavailable under this reading; it does not independently establish an approval obligation or non-compliance. Unknown inputs remain unknown. Continuing notification and post-vetting obligations are outside this predicate.","subject":"Eligibility of a selected material UCITS investment change for removal of SFC prior approval"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.074087c89e3a3304960f612e","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"3ba4bde717985a09f564d0eff99c12ebad94a746720bac76452ef3844383c5a0","candidate_id":"candidate.bdaa269bb59a475abb823352d859db65","commitment":"4d548f2e09bc36ef51212f641bb766ca0dc8cad771472770f91918b6061fb78e","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.4d548f2e09bc36ef51212f64","order":2,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The express Effective Date supplies the date intended by the introductory immediate-effect language.","The selected formal control excludes applications caught by the transition, because their treatment requires the existing process and missing FAQs.","The introductory reference to home supervision describes the measures' purpose; it is not treated as an additional independently specified condition in item (ii)."],"citations":[{"quote":"The key streamlined measures cover the following post-authorisation matters:","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"},{"quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"quote":"1 For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"}],"distinction":"The text supports a clear removal-of-approval eligibility rule for changes outside the transition, rather than rival conjunctive and disjunctive exception rules. For example, an ordinary home-compliant investment-policy change in a covered Irish UCITS after the Effective Date qualifies if it has no possible local policy implications; the same change with possible local policy implications does not qualify even if it is neither novel nor complex. For an otherwise identical application received on 27 November 2025 and pending at transition, existing processing applies and this formal control gives no answer. The strongest uncertainty is whether that preserved processing also necessarily preserves the substantive approval prerequisite.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The fund is a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a UK-domiciled collective investment scheme authorised as UK UCITS, within the circular's definition.","name":"covered_ucits","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change is a post-authorisation material change to the fund's investment objective, policy or restriction.","name":"covered_material_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u3.575","d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The date as of which availability of the circular's approval removal is assessed; this does not select an implementation-date test for every transitional situation.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"An application concerning this change was received by the SFC before 28 November 2025 and remained without approval or authorisation at the Effective Date.","name":"pending_legacy_application","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed investment change complies with the fund's applicable home-jurisdiction requirements.","name":"home_requirements_met","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change involves novel product features.","name":"novel_features","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change involves complex product features.","name":"complex_features","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The assessed change may have local policy implications; actual realised implications are not required by this wording.","name":"possible_local_policy_implications","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and home_requirements_met (not (or novel_features complex_features possible_local_policy_implications)))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and covered_ucits covered_material_change (>= assessment_date (date 2025-11-28)) (not pending_legacy_application))"},"local_id":"approval_removal_eligibility","questions":["For a pending legacy application, does existing processing require approval before the change can take effect, or only govern disposition of the already-filed application?","What evidence and interpretive standards establish home compliance and the absence of each exception under the missing FAQs?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Selected control: eligibility for removal of prior SFC approval for a material UCITS investment change outside the legacy-application transition. Within the stated scope, true means the change meets the circular's stated home-compliance condition and none of its stated exceptions applies. False means this removal is unavailable under those conditions; it does not independently establish a prohibition, non-compliance or the complete underlying approval obligation. Outside scope, the result supplies no determination. Unknown facts remain unknown.","subject":"Prior-approval removal for material changes to UCITS investment objectives, policies or restrictions"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.4d548f2e09bc36ef51212f64","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"5874936c74418d89b087db7f12194a7b2cb15c2c137438a9d5e53c2beb513c94","candidate_id":"candidate.cde02cf9d56c44e6a6ec9dc55ebcda36","commitment":"4e6a162c35678e9ddf17ad8e25adc2015b890fa1601cff818fbbc2f5a6da765a","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.4e6a162c35678e9ddf17ad8e","order":3,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The assessment concerns one identified material change to an SFC-authorised fund’s investment objective, policy or restriction.","Product-feature and local-policy tests concern the proposed change, including features it introduces or alters, rather than an unrelated feature of the fund.","An application received before 28 November 2025 and still unapproved or unauthorised at the transition remains in the existing process; it is not treated as eligible to bypass that process through the new removal measure.","Failure to qualify for this removal does not, by itself, establish an independently applicable prior-approval obligation."],"citations":[{"quote":"(ii)       Material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions – Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"quote":"1 For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"}],"distinction":"Eligibility for removal of prior approval depends on both the change’s substantive components and the procedural history of its application. A single fund-level Boolean would hide change-specific exceptions and the pending-application transition. Removal also leaves post-vetting distinct from prior approval.","family":"exceptions","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The fund is a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands.","name":"covered_eu_ucits","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the assessed fund"},{"meaning":"The fund is a collective investment scheme domiciled in the United Kingdom and authorised as UK UCITS.","name":"covered_uk_ucits","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the assessed fund"},{"meaning":"The assessed change is a post-authorisation matter for an SFC-authorised fund.","name":"post_authorisation_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u3.575"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the assessed change"},{"meaning":"The assessed change materially changes at least one investment objective, policy or restriction of the fund.","name":"material_investment_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the assessed change"},{"meaning":"Date at which reliance on the removal measure is assessed for the proposed implementation.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The assessed change satisfies all home-jurisdiction requirements applicable to that change.","name":"home_requirements_satisfied","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value across applicable home requirements"},{"meaning":"At least one product feature involved in the assessed change is novel.","name":"involves_novel_feature","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for features involved in the change"},{"meaning":"At least one product feature involved in the assessed change is complex.","name":"involves_complex_feature","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for features involved in the change"},{"meaning":"The assessed change may have local policy implications; actual realised implications are not required.","name":"may_have_local_policy_implications","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the assessed change"},{"meaning":"There exists an application concerning the assessed change that the SFC received before 28 November 2025 and for which neither approval nor authorisation had been granted at the transition.","name":"pending_pre_effective_application","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809","d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value over related applications at transition"}],"result":"(and home_requirements_satisfied (not involves_novel_feature) (not involves_complex_feature) (not may_have_local_policy_implications) (not pending_pre_effective_application))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and (or covered_eu_ucits covered_uk_ucits) post_authorisation_change material_investment_change (>= assessment_date (date 2025-11-28)))"},"local_id":"prior_approval_removal_eligibility","questions":["What are the fund’s domicile, UCITS status and, if UK-domiciled, UK UCITS authorisation status?","What components of the proposed change affect investment objectives, policies or restrictions, and why is the change material?","Does the change comply with each applicable home-jurisdiction requirement, and does it involve novel or complex product features or possible local policy implications?","When is the change being assessed for implementation, and was a related application received before 28 November 2025 with no approval or authorisation granted at the transition?","What do the referenced FAQs and existing approval process provide about the underlying approval obligation and treatment of pending applications?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within scope, true means the assessed change qualifies for this circular’s removal of prior SFC approval, subject to the stated transition interpretation. False means that removal is unavailable under this model, not that the change is prohibited or that an independent prior-approval obligation has been established. Outside scope no conclusion is supplied. Unknown inputs remain unknown. This result confers no legal approval.","subject":"Eligibility of a material UCITS investment change for removal of prior SFC approval"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.4e6a162c35678e9ddf17ad8e","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"97d235517bef97dc0bdd7e00af7c370fc9d761d5e28d3921cd11296abbcca095","candidate_id":"candidate.cb18463f57a84378b0dba5b3cd3e87bc","commitment":"ce439b1cf9ed8301fbb68f94b033da6c17a7f2b7cd33b6ebc6a3bb3b0dfd32ae","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.ce439b1cf9ed8301fbb68f94","order":4,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The specific Effective Date of 28 November 2025 governs the general statement that the measures take immediate effect.","The assessment concerns one identified material post-authorisation change, including every product feature involved in that change.","The transition preserves the existing process for the application covering this change if it was received before the Effective Date and remained unapproved or unauthorised at that date.","Failure to qualify for removal does not independently establish a prior-approval obligation; that conclusion requires the applicable existing rules."],"citations":[{"quote":"For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"quote":"The SFC will continue to conduct post-vetting of scheme changes (including those not subject to the SFC’s prior approval) and related revised documents filed with the SFC.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u12.2069"}],"distinction":"Eligibility attaches to a particular change, while the transition attaches to its application and decision history. Home compliance, novel features, complex features and possible local policy implications are separate tests. Removal of prior approval does not remove post-vetting or establish overall compliance.","family":"time","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The fund is a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands.","name":"listed_european_ucits","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the fund"},{"meaning":"The fund is a collective investment scheme domiciled in the United Kingdom and authorised as UK UCITS.","name":"uk_ucits","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the fund"},{"meaning":"The identified change concerns an already SFC-authorised fund in a post-authorisation matter.","name":"post_authorisation_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u3.575"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the change"},{"meaning":"The identified change is material and changes at least one investment objective, policy or restriction.","name":"material_investment_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the change"},{"meaning":"The identified change complies with the fund’s applicable home jurisdiction requirements.","name":"home_requirements_met","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the change under home requirements"},{"meaning":"At least one product feature involved in the identified change is novel.","name":"involves_novel_feature","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value across all features involved in the change"},{"meaning":"At least one product feature involved in the identified change is complex.","name":"involves_complex_feature","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value across all features involved in the change"},{"meaning":"The identified change may have local policy implications; actual realised implications are not required.","name":"may_have_local_policy_implications","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for possible implications of the change"},{"meaning":"Date for which availability of the circular’s removal of prior approval is assessed.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"There exists an application covering the identified change that the SFC received before 28 November 2025 and for which neither approval nor authorisation had been granted at that date. False includes absence of such an application.","name":"pending_pre_effective_application","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the application history of the change"}],"result":"(and (>= assessment_date (date 2025-11-28)) home_requirements_met (not involves_novel_feature) (not involves_complex_feature) (not may_have_local_policy_implications) (not pending_pre_effective_application))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and (or listed_european_ucits uk_ucits) post_authorisation_change material_investment_change)"},"local_id":"removal_eligibility","questions":["What are the fund’s domicile, UCITS status and, if applicable, UK UCITS authorisation status?","What change is proposed, is it material, and does it concern an investment objective, policy or restriction of an already authorised fund?","Does the change comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, and does any feature involved qualify as novel or complex or potentially carry local policy implications?","On what date is the removal being assessed, and was an application covering this change received before 28 November 2025 and still awaiting approval or authorisation at that date?","What do the referenced FAQs and existing approval process require, including for applications preserved by the transition?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within scope, true means the identified change qualifies for this circular’s removal of the SFC prior-approval requirement on the assessment date. False means at least one removal condition fails, including the application transition; it does not by itself establish that prior approval is required. Unknown facts remain unknown. This is a proposed eligibility interpretation, not legal approval.","subject":"Eligibility for removal of prior SFC approval for a material UCITS investment change"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.ce439b1cf9ed8301fbb68f94","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0},{"bundle_hash":"87a2b103adc1f70a21ebe4a5f2caf045f9de460ade098c4cf6e809b56b2cf6e9","candidate_id":"candidate.9a2722ba25c64e2f993dc51efb82a5a7","commitment":"b66b3e831bb98a12db59dffac2ebe6afa2f91f2ad8eff7222273f4d126b17f69","depth":0,"disposition":"UNREVIEWED","encoding_error":null,"expanded":false,"issued_calls":0,"node_id":"node.b66b3e831bb98a12db59dffa","order":5,"parent":null,"reading":{"assumptions":["The assessment concerns one identified material post-authorisation investment change to an SFC-authorised fund within the circular’s UCITS definition.","All product features involved in the identified change are assessed; the source supplies no rule for severing a bundled change.","28 November 2025 governs commencement of the removal measure.","The transition preserves the process for an existing application; it does not expressly make application history an additional substantive exception to the removal measure.","Substantive qualification for removal does not establish permission to bypass a preserved application process or establish overall legal compliance."],"citations":[{"quote":"Removing the SFC’s requirement on prior approval for material changes in investment objectives, policies and restrictions which comply with the fund’s home jurisdiction requirements, except for changes that involve novel or complex product features and/or which may have local policy implications.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u5.840"},{"quote":"Existing applications received by the SFC before the Effective Date for which no approval or authorisation has been granted will be processed by the SFC in accordance with the existing approval or authorisation process.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u10.1809"},{"quote":"The streamlined measures set out in the relevant FAQs will take effect on 28 November 2025 (Effective Date).","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"},{"quote":"For this circular, UCITS funds means (i) Undertakings for Collective Investment in Transferable Securities (UCITS) domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland and the Netherlands, and (ii) collective investment schemes domiciled in the United Kingdom authorised as UK UCITS.","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"},{"quote":"The key streamlined measures cover the following post-authorisation matters:","unit_id":"d97b56331f41a.u3.575"}],"distinction":"Both prior models turn existence of a pending pre-effective application into a change-level removal veto. This rival distinguishes the substantive conditions attached to a change from the process attached to an application. A substantively qualifying change can coexist with an application that must follow the existing process. The prior models already identify the main actors and feature quantifiers; the consequential issue is the relation between application history and the legal effect being computed, including later application decisions.","family":"dependencies","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The assessed fund is either a UCITS domiciled in France, Luxembourg, Ireland or the Netherlands, or a United Kingdom-domiciled collective investment scheme authorised as UK UCITS.","name":"covered_ucits","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u17.2556"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the fund"},{"meaning":"The identified change is a post-authorisation matter for an already SFC-authorised fund.","name":"post_authorisation_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u3.575"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the change"},{"meaning":"The identified change materially alters at least one investment objective, policy or restriction of the fund.","name":"material_investment_change","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for the change"},{"meaning":"Date for which the substantive removal conditions are assessed.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u9.1696"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"The identified change satisfies every home-jurisdiction requirement applicable to that change.","name":"home_requirements_met","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value across applicable home requirements"},{"meaning":"At least one product feature involved in the identified change is novel.","name":"involves_novel_feature","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value across involved product features"},{"meaning":"At least one product feature involved in the identified change is complex.","name":"involves_complex_feature","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value across involved product features"},{"meaning":"The identified change may have local policy implications, whether or not those implications have actually occurred.","name":"possible_local_policy_implications","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d97b56331f41a.u5.840"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value for possible implications of the change"}],"result":"(and home_requirements_met (not involves_novel_feature) (not involves_complex_feature) (not possible_local_policy_implications))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and covered_ucits post_authorisation_change material_investment_change (>= assessment_date (date 2025-11-28)))"},"local_id":"substantive_conditions_separate_from_application_process","questions":["What are the fund’s domicile, UCITS classification and, where relevant, UK UCITS authorisation status?","Which objectives, policies, restrictions and product features are involved in the identified material change?","Does the change meet every applicable home-jurisdiction requirement, involve any novel or complex feature, or possibly have local policy implications?","Which application covers which change components, when did the SFC receive it, and what decisions had been granted at the Effective Date and by the assessment date?","Do the referenced FAQs make preservation of an application’s existing process a bar to substantive removal, and how do they treat subsequent decisions, amendments, withdrawal or resubmission?","What existing rules determine whether prior approval is required when the substantive removal conditions are not met?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Within scope, true means the identified change satisfies the substantive home-requirements and exception tests in item (ii); false means at least one of those tests fails. The result answers only that substantive question. It does not answer whether a pending application can leave the existing process or whether prior approval is legally required in the particular procedural circumstances. Outside scope no conclusion is supplied. Unknown facts remain unknown. This proposal confers no legal approval.","subject":"Substantive removal conditions distinguished from preservation of an application’s existing process"},"repair_needed":false,"reward":0,"root":"node.b66b3e831bb98a12db59dffa","roundtrip_done":false,"visits":0}],"pending":null,"provider_id":"codex.fresh.v1.compact.v2","retrievals":[],"rounds":0,"roundtrips":[],"run_id":"run.319c058876aa4441a4b41af39001d48a","stop":null}